body:
Seems reasonable, but do we want to preserve `ERR_FILE_NOT_FOUND` detection? If we do, it can get `pid` from `create_process` and wait for a half second or so:

```c++
ProcessID pid = 0;
Error ok = create_process("xdg-open", args, &pid);
if (ok == OK) {
    uint64_t t = get_ticks_usec();
    do {
        if (get_process_exit_code(pid) == 2) {
            return ERR_FILE_NOT_FOUND;
        }
    } while (get_ticks_usec() - t < 200000);
    return OK;
}
```
